the knowledge base chapter 61 includes these resources:
    section_xi.

the knowledge base chapter 61 includes:

rule knitted_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6117
    and the subheading group of the good is a group
    and the gender of the good is a gender
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the component has a fabric for heading the heading
    and the fibre material of the component is a material
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the group of the gender in the material is the code under table knitted.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1). Note 1: only knitted or crocheted articles.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule heading_6101 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Men's or boys' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski-jackets), windbreakers and similar articles, knitted or crocheted, other than those of heading 6103":
a garment is described by heading 6101
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the family of the garment is outerwear.

rule heading_6102 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Women's or girls' overcoats, carcoats, capes, cloaks, anoraks (including ski-jackets), windbreakers and similar articles, knitted or crocheted, other than those of heading 6104":
a garment is described by heading 6102
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the family of the garment is outerwear.

rule heading_6103 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Men's or boys' suits, ensembles, suit-type jackets, blazers, trousers, bib and brace overalls, breeches and shorts (other than swimwear), knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6103
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the subheading group of the garment is a group
    and the group is in [suit, ensemble, suit-type jacket, trousers].

rule heading_6104 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Women's or girls' suits, ensembles, suit-type jackets, blazers, dresses, skirts, divided skirts, trousers, bib and brace overalls, breeches and shorts (other than swimwear), knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6104
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the subheading group of the garment is a group
    and the group is in [suit, ensemble, suit-type jacket, dress, skirt, trousers].

rule heading_6105 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Men's or boys' shirts, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6105
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the garment is a shirt.

rule heading_6106 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Women's or girls' blouses and shirts, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6106
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the garment is a blouse-type garment.

rule heading_6107 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Men's or boys' underpants, briefs, nightshirts, pajamas, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6107
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is men
    and the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [underpants, nightwear, robe].

rule heading_6108 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Women's or girls' slips, petticoats, briefs, panties, night dresses, pajamas, negligees, bathrobes, dressing gowns and similar articles, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6108
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the gender of the garment is women
    and the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [slip, underpants, nightwear, robe].

rule heading_6109 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "T-shirts, singlets, tank tops and similar garments, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6109
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the garment is of the T-shirt family.

% The Explanatory Note to heading 6110: a category of knitted articles, without
% distinction as to sex, designed to cover the upper parts of the body.
% the Explanatory Note to heading 6110 (Sweaters, pullovers, sweatshirts,
% waistcoats and similar articles, knitted or crocheted), as a French BTI
% quotes it
rule heading_6110 with provenance BTI FRBTIFR-BTI-2025-06897,
        confer "la présente position couvre une catégorie d'articles en bonneterie, sans distinction quant au sexe, destinés à recouvrir la partie supérieure du corps":
a garment is described by heading 6110
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the garment is a top.

rule heading_6111 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Babies' garments and clothing accessories, knitted or crocheted":
a good is described by heading 6111
    if the construction of the good is knitted
    and the good is sized for babies.

rule heading_6112 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Track suits, ski-suits and swimwear, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6112
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the family of the garment is a family
    and the family is in [track suit, ski-suit, swimwear].

rule heading_6113 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Garments, made up of knitted or crocheted fabrics of heading 5903, 5906 or 5907":
a garment is described by heading 6113
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the garment is a garment
    and the garment is made up of fabric of heading a heading
    and the heading is in [5903, 5906, 5907].

rule heading_6114 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Other garments, knitted or crocheted":
a garment is described by heading 6114
    if the construction of the garment is knitted
    and the garment is a garment.

rule heading_6115 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Panty hose, tights, stockings, socks and other hosiery, including graduated compression hosiery":
a good is described by heading 6115
    if the construction of the good is knitted
    and the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [panty hose, hosiery].

rule heading_6116 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Gloves, mittens and mitts, knitted or crocheted":
a good is described by heading 6116
    if the construction of the good is knitted
    and the family of the good is gloves.

rule heading_6117 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Other made up clothing accessories, knitted or crocheted; knitted or crocheted parts of garments or of clothing accessories":
a good is described by heading 6117
    if the construction of the good is knitted
    and the family of the good is a family
    and the family is in [scarf, handkerchief, tie, other accessory, part].

% The exclusions of notes 4 and 5 (section_xi.le has the shirt headings').
rule note_61_5 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Heading 6109 does not cover garments with a drawstring, ribbed waistband or other means of tightening at the bottom of the garment":
a garment is excluded from heading 6109
    if the garment has a means of tightening at the bottom.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Choosing between headings that both describe a good (GRI 3(a) in gri.le).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Note 6(b): babies' garments and accessories go to heading 6111, whatever
% other heading of the chapter also describes them.
rule note_61_6b_before with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Articles which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6111 and in other headings of this chapter are to be classified in heading 6111":
heading 6111 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6110.

rule note_61_6b_after with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Articles which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6111 and in other headings of this chapter are to be classified in heading 6111":
heading 6111 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6112
    and the heading <= 6117.

% Note 8: garments of coated fabric go to heading 6113, unless they are
% babies' garments.
rule note_61_8_before with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Garments which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6113 and in other headings of this chapter, excluding heading 6111, are to be classified in heading 6113":
heading 6113 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6110.

rule note_61_8_after with provenance HTSUS Chapter 61,
        confer "Garments which are, prima facie, classifiable both in heading 6113 and in other headings of this chapter, excluding heading 6111, are to be classified in heading 6113":
heading 6113 is more specific than heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6114
    and the heading <= 6117.

% Heading 6114 ("other garments") covers what the headings before it do not:
% each of them is the more specific description.
rule gri_3a_6114 with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description":
heading a heading is more specific than heading 6114
    if the heading >= 6101
    and the heading <= 6112.

% GRI 3(a) between the headings of tops. Heading 6110 names a category ("...
% and similar articles") of which shirts, blouses and T-shirts are particular
% kinds; and CBP holds a loose-fitting women's top to be a blouse rather than a
% T-shirt.
% a shirt is a particular kind of the upper-body garments of heading 6110
heading 6105 is more specific than heading 6110,
    as stated in HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation, confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description".
% a blouse or shirt is a particular kind of the upper-body garments of heading
% 6110
heading 6106 is more specific than heading 6110,
    as stated in HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation, confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description".
% a T-shirt, tank top or singlet is a particular kind of the upper-body
% garments of heading 6110
heading 6109 is more specific than heading 6110,
    as stated in HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation, confer "The heading which provides the most specific description shall be preferred to headings providing a more general description".
% loose-fitting women's tops have the characteristics of blouses of Note 4 to
% Chapter 61, which precludes headings 6109 and 6110
heading 6106 is more specific than heading 6109,
    according to CBP, as stated in ruling NY N356079, confer "in accordance with the reasoning set forth in Headquarters Ruling Letters H325360 and H324935".
